From 09e597fd3d23a9878ed4ec2fc2b4856c8bc9b3e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 20:15:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Data: audit every fluid capacity, fix three more wrong
 figures
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The F-150 rear differential error found earlier today turned out not to be
a one-off. Normalized all 41 capacity figures in the catalog to a common
unit and checked every outlier against a real source.

The differentials were systematically wrong:

- Silverado and Sierra rear axle read ~3.4 pt (1.6 L). The AAM 9.76-inch
  axle takes about 5.5 pt (2.75 qt). Roughly 40% low, and note the F-150's
  9.75-inch axle carried the identical 1.6 L figure before today's fix —
  all three trucks appear to have come from the same bad basis.
- Their rear axle spec also said 75W-90. GM's own fill spec for the
  1500-series rear axle is 75W-85 (GM 19300457). 75W-90 is a workable
  substitute but should not be listed as the spec.
- The Jeep's rear axle figure survives, but published values for the WK2
  range from about 0.95 to 1.5 qt depending on axle and drivetrain, so it
  is now shown as a range rather than a single number.

Every differential entry now also carries the fill-to-the-bottom-of-the-
fill-plug-hole instruction. That is the actual factory procedure and it is
self-correcting, which matters on a component where published capacities
disagree and underfilling destroys the unit.

Separately, the Escape's engine oil was wrong twice over. The 2021 Escape
owner's manual specifies 5.3 qt (5.05 L) of SAE 5W-20 synthetic blend
meeting API SP. This file had 5.7 qt of 0W-20 full synthetic — a 0.4 qt
overfill and the wrong viscosity.

Checked and correct, no change: engine oil on the Jeep, Civic, F-150,
Silverado and Sierra; front differentials on all three trucks; every
transmission, transfer case, coolant and washer figure.

Verified: next build compiles clean; all 13 guides pass every required
check; eslint unchanged at the same 4 pre-existing problems.

